# Candidate A evidence: durable Lavish answer-receipt lifecycle

Capture branch: `fm/fm-lavish-receipt-state-a`
Code head producing this evidence: `ebdb2fa274e267246d7f0bb0db47077ec1792767`
This directory (screenshots, demo artifact, this manifest) is delivery evidence
committed on top of that head; it contains no code.

Note on the commits after capture: one internal race was closed first (a
concurrent reconcile could rarely duplicate a capture's internal announcement
before the receipt seam acknowledged it; the per-source boundary now spans
capture through the seam). Rebuilding this work on moved upstream then added
two compatibility fixes - macOS ancestor symlinks (`/tmp` and `/var` through
`/private`) no longer fail procevent private-directory validation, and the
managed delivery poll now runs through the adapter's shared quiet-retry loop -
and two review fixes hardening the receipts record and staging cleanup and
presenting a round's receipt once instead of re-sending it on a quiet retry.
None of them changes visible receipt text or page layout, so the screenshots
below match the delivered behavior and the reproduction steps below remain
valid.

